{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/934945-post-some-of-your-pcs-you-have-starting-level-please","id":934945,"title":"Post some of YOUR pcs you have (starting level please)..","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-21T00:46:59-07:00","id":934945,"title":"Post some of YOUR pcs you have (starting level please)..","content":"Since i mentioned about it on the thread on werewolves being the best fighters?? i decided to make this thread on showing or builds for some of the starting PCs we all have..<br /> <br /> Here is my current actual LIST of characters (Starting, not including my Vampires as they were made with the age and generation HR i posted earlier in the VtM sub-forum)..<br /> All were made BTB..<br /> Garou<br /> Jo'hn Marrik, Bone Gnawer metis Philodox<br /> Kort, Child of Gaia Lupus Theurge<br /> Thuthket McFadden, Fianna metis Ahroun<br /> Bryon Bryant, Glass walker Homid Ragbash<br /> Gwar, Red Talon Lupus Ahroun<br /> Croll &quot;paws the mud&quot; Shadowlord Lupus Ahroun<br /> Hazzeem Khalzaill, Silent strider metis Ragbash.<br /> Sharr &quot;Blade wind, Silver fang metis Ahroun (klaive dueler)<br /> Tutakka Swift bite, Wendigo Lupus Galliard<br /> Windtalker, Wendigo metis Theurge<br /> <br /> Other Fera<br /> Darren &quot;Silent teeth', Balam Metis, Night<br /> Shiro Hirutsu, Khan Daylight, Feline (made for a Hengeyokai game that never got off the ground)<br /> Milp, Forest walker Arcas Ursine<br /> Borda &quot;Smacks his foes, River keeper ursine Umzati<br /> Vakar &quot;Flies to Helios&quot; Mokole-mbembe, Suchid, warding<br /> and M'hras Long claw, Mokole-mbembe suchid Rising sun.<br /> <br /> Others (mortals)<br /> Berrin Thaddsonn. Get Kinfolk (homid)<br /> Shiro Tetsuki, Shih wanderer..<br /> <br /> <br /> For the characters, i will post 2 at a time (giving 3-4 days between them, to allow others to chime in if they wish..)<br /> <br /> John Marrik, Metis Philodox of the Bone Gnawers. Street cop template, with the Hoods camp. Metis disfigurement of no Hispo form due to both parents being homids.<br /> Str 2, Dex 4 (swift), Stamina 4 (resiliant), Charisma 2, Appearance 2, Manipulation 2, Perception 4 (keen eyed), Intelligence 2, Wits 2<br /> Alertness 2, Athletics 1, Brawl 2, dodge, 2, Empathy 1, Intimidation 1, Primal urge 1, Streetwise 3, Animal ken 1, Firearms 2, Melee 2, Repair 1, Stealth 2, Survival 1, Investigations 1, Law 1, Lingquistics 1 (italian), Rituals 1, occult 1.<br /> Has Gifts of resist toxin, scent of true form and sense wyrm.<br /> Backrounds: Ally 2, Contacts 2, Fetish 3, Rites 1, Totem 1. (4 freebies spent) [ Ritual known Talisman dedication).<br /> Rage 5 (2 freebies), Gnosis 6 (6 freebies), Willpower 6 (3 freebies).<br /> Fetish - Leech tongue<br /> Merits and flaws taken -<br /> Merits Charmed existance (5 cost), Local ties (Police) 3<br /> Flaws- pack mentality +2, Oath of Osiris (one of my home made ones) +5.<br /> Contacts, Derrick O'konnel, Pawn broker and Carrine Tristy, Mortician.<br /> Allies Jean Sanderson, Reporter for Sun sport, and Luc Dupoit, fellow cop.<br /> <br /> <br /> Kort, Lupus Theurge Child of gaia, School watch dog concept, no camp.<br /> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3, Charisma 1, Appearance 1, Manipulation 4 (Persuasive), Perception 3, Intelligence 3, Wits 4 (practical)<br /> Alertness 2, Brawl 2, Dodge 3, Empathy 3, Expression 2, Primal urge 2, Animal ken 2, Melee 1, Leadership 1, Performance 2, Stealth 2, Survial 1, Rituals 3, Occult 2, Medicine 2, Linguistics 1 (english). (6 freebies spent)<br /> Has gifts of Heightened sense, mothers touch and sense wyrm<br /> Backrounds: Rites 4, Ally 1, Kinfolk 1 [Rituals known Spirit summoning, Talisman dedication, Cleansing] (1 freebie spent)<br /> Rage 4 (2 freebies spent), Gnosis 7 (4 freebies spent), Willpower 7 (4 freebies spent)<br /> Merits and flaws =<br /> Merit Charmed existance (5 point cost)<br /> Flaws - Banned transformation (must spend rage to do so +3), Curiosity +2, Soft hearted +1, No partial transformation +1<br /> Ally is School vet<br /> Kin is a homid cousin who is a Custodian at the same school.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T14:50:53-07:00","id":936256,"title":"","content":"Strange. I would have thought i might get at least a comment or two, or even someone posting one of their pcs by now..<br /> <br /> Oh well..<br /> Onto my next 2 pcs.<br /> <br /> First up i wil do the kinfolk Berrin Thaddson.<br /> Being Get kin, he went with phys as his pri, so all three of Str/Dex/Stam are 3 dots each, Social got evened out at 2 apiece, while Mental was secondary giving him a 3 wits and perception and 2 intelligence.<br /> <br /> Talents were primary (11 dots, +1 from freebies), giving im a 2 alertness, streetwise and dodge, 3 Brawl and 1 each in indimidatio, athletics and intuition.<br /> Skills pulled in 2nd (7 dots +2 from freebies), giving him 1 drive and leadership, 2 in melee and stealth and 3 firearms.<br /> Knowledges was tertiary (4 dots no freebies spent), giving him 1 in investigation and linguistics (spanish), and 2 medicine.<br /> Backrounds were split between equipment (3 dots) and resources (2 dots),<br /> Additional freebies went to get other skills/talents from the Players HB, (2 in throwing, demolitiions and gunsmithing for 12 more freebies spent, bring the total to 18 so far)<br /> Willpower was raised from 3 to 8 (10 more freebies..<br /> He has only flaws (no merits) giving him 7 more freebies to spend, covering the remaining needed for his willpower increase. They are Maschicist (1), mild phobia of snakes (1) and veiled (5)..<br /> <br /> Then we move onto one of my other mortals, a Project twilight FBI agent..<br /> Douglas Sandars. <br /> Being a field agent he went Phys/ment/soci for his attributes, with 3s in all the physicals, and 2s for all the socials, and his mental breakdown was int and per 3, wits 2.<br /> Talents was secondary for his abilities pick (7 dots worth +2 dots from freebies), with a spread of 2 alertness and brawling, and 1 athletics, intimidation, leadership, streetwise and subterfuge.<br /> Skills was primary, (11 dots worth +2 dots from freebies), with 4 in firearms, 2 in each of stealth and repair, and one in drive, security and survival,<br /> For knowledges he went with 1 in covert culture, law and occult and 2 in investigations (spending 2 more freebies to get that 5th dot).<br /> Backrounds were where the majority of his freebies went, giving him 3 in allies and resources, 2 in influence and rank, and 4 in equipment. <br /> He took some merits (agency insider 3 points) and license to kill (2 points), but offset them with some flaws (Primary bread winner, 2 points), child (1 point) and Siege mentality (3 points.)..<br /> The remainder was used to bump his willpower up to 7..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T08:57:46-07:00","id":937115,"title":"","content":"I use the nWoD system so I'm not sure how interested you might be in the few characters I have that could be put here; but I do have two or three Vampires I could put and talk about, I think they both followed V20 or so; not nWoD at any rate. I wonder though if I should go into detail on why the stats are the way they are cuz a lot seems to be just character building without explaining why the dots are as they are. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T11:30:54-07:00","id":937185,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Adam Black Phd. Eco (Ventrue M)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Concept: Honorable &amp; famous Ecologist who has become friends the primogen as he has become an expert on the traditions and vampire laws. Infact the six traditions and especially the Ventrue concept of Dignitas is the Code of honor you follow. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is just one problem... or two\u2026 your ex-wife that left you due to your work and lack of time has married again and her new husband is a hunter. Yesterday was their marriage ceremony and while you thought you could pull it off you didn\u2019t. Now you are the #1 target for the whole hunter group - and his wife is a member.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your love goes so deep your feeding restriction is a caricature of what your wife was, a lawyer.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Goals: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Short term: Trying to deal with the hunter attacks that might follow</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Medium term: using the primogen to gain a permit to either sire yourself or let someone else sire a person of your choice</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Long term: Persuade or otherwise force your wife to be sired, repair the masquerade breach that she and her s.o. cause, &quot;deal&quot; with him</span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/korlb8yvr2uha34/Adam%20Black%20Phd.%20Eco.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/korlb8yvr2uha34/Adam%20Black%20Phd.%20Eco.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/korlb8yvr2...20Eco.pdf?dl=0</a></u></span></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Akia bint Tariq bin Al-Fulan (Assamite F)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Concept: A Assamite lady-killer who started falling from the path of blood. When you started you threw yourself into the path of blood and Haqim. You understood fast, but the more you understood the less you felt that the Assamites were actually following his spirit. You were groomed early, as you were able to resist blood magic more than many others, but all of this just made you restless. Slowly but surely you knew you were wrong here and searched for answers. A mission led you to NY and you met Lucinde, the Justicar of the Ventrue. She saw great potential in you and lured you further and further away from the Assamites. As you saw how she judged vampires and how magnificent she was in all her magnificence you were sure. You would have to join her in her quest. You left the assamites and joined the Carmarilla. Now everyone more or less hates you, but Lucinde became a tip that a Anathema is in this city. You just have to look for her.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Goals:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Short term: Search for clues in the city. Help Lucinde stay undercover by reporting everything and judging people</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Medium term: Help your mentor and further her cause with the prince of the city</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Long term: either find a new path of enlightenment that fits better to you or fix the Path of Blood so you are able to exist as you are.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/iotkefcpq1gd3h2/Akia%20bint%20Tariq%20bin%20Al-Fulan.pdf?dl=0</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alejandro Lopez (Ventrue M)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Concept: You are the scourge. You and your ghoul Max are the guys they send if the thin bloods are sighted. People know, you might have a bit of a cruel strain in you, but nothing major. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While you are a good fighter you have a secret not many know, your wounds do not really heal as well as they should, your sire had the same problems so you did never really think about it, but nowadays you wonder what happened there. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As you started as the scourge the childer of the Gangrel primogen helped you tremendously. One night you both were attacked by two dozens of thin bloods and while you were able to escape, he did not. You did not see how, but someone killed him there. He was a much better fighter than you, so that did never make sense to you. The primogen and the whole clan think it is your fault and hate you for it. Now there are not that many Gangrel in the city itself, but you know that you have to watch your back big time. You even heard that your reputation has reached other cities as well. Oh boy. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Goals:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Short term: deal with the thin bloods</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Medium term: Something was off that night. Maybe you should do some research to what has really happened there - but the only ones who would know are the thin bloods! You still have some pull at your local police department, might as well ask there.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Long term: Clear your name before you get killed. Gangrel are not to be trifled with.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ann Thorper (Setite F)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Concept: You pray upon the people when they are weak and that is what they are when one of their relatives just died. As a cemetery owner you let your ghoul and herd do most of the stuff that is needed to run the company, what you want are the people. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Infact you stay clearly away of your own home as you are a magnet for werewolves for some reason. Not only that you share their vulnerability for silver as well.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Too many coincidences for your own taste, but what can anyone do against it? Something is off here, but you need more information. You need someone that is an expert\u2026 but would you trust anyone with such a weakness?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Short term: find a coterie, does not matter who!</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Medium term: get someone to make your home werewolf secure, at all costs</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Long term: explore the reasons for your connection with the werewolfs</span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/r1d8a2g2l0h40fq/Alejandro%20Lopez.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/r1d8a2g2l0h40fq/Alejandro%20Lopez.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/r1d8a2g2l0...Lopez.pdf?dl=0</a></u></span></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Barbara Stone (City Gangrel F)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Concept: You are an ex-shovel head that survived, since then you trained to survive and you are now a fighting machine. Your pack knows this and lets you enjoy it and the Carmarilla hates you so much that they formed a war coterie just to kill you. Let them come.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The bigger problem you see is not on the fighting side anyway. Against Gangrel philosophy you took interest in the politics of the sect and you start to feel bad about it. You did not bud heads yet, but who knows what will happen in the future.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Short term: learn more about survivability, it is an actual spot on your record</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Medium term: learn more about the agenda of your bishop, evade the war coterie</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Long term: Annihilate said coterie one by one, start to become a major political player if possible</span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/zzr0nhx0bc3rjb8/Barbara%20Stone.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/zzr0nhx0bc3rjb8/Barbara%20Stone.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/zzr0nhx0bc...Stone.pdf?dl=0</a></u></span></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Christian Braun (Hunter M)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Concept: German bodyguard moved to the US who seeks his vampire wife Olivia. One night his wife leaves to jog around but never comes back. Since then he is searching for her and after a while he even found her. Kind of. She is now the Childer of a local high ranking vampire and is under his influence. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shocked about this revelation he stumbled into a catholic church, as his religiosity comes through. Willing to do everything in his power and desperate he confesses to the priest who thinks he is crazy and screams for help. Christian leaves the booth in tears but gets stopped very quickly, as two rather muscular looking stand in front of him. They are hunters from the Society of Leopold and want to kill Olivia's sire. They don\u2019t want Christian involved, but after a bit of time he is able to convince them that he at least is able to provide intelligence and observational skills. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Short term: Observe closely and report to your Hunter group every step the vampires make</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Medium term: Get them to accept you</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Long term: Find a solution to your wife's \u201cproblem\u201d</span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/6tswzbnhjxy91sm/Christian%20Braun.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/6tswzbnhjxy91sm/Christian%20Braun.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/6tswzbnhjx...Braun.pdf?dl=0</a></u></span></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Colin MacLachlan (Gangrel M)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Concept: Colin is a hard-nosed, misanthropic loan shark. Before he was embraced his sire almost killed him and his wounds are permanent, because his sires \u201ckiss\u201d hurt so much that he screamed in agony and tried to stop it. Another thing he inherited. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">His predatory nature is mostly focused in humans. He preys on the weak and wrings them out for the money they have. His sire made him to get a pawn in the streetgame and after a while he rose in the ranks of organized crime. Him and his ghouls control most of the loan sharking in the city. He pays tribute to the higher ups, but he really starts to dislike that. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Short term: Fathom if it is possible to gain more independence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Medium term: Create a power base so you can be more independent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Long term: Become a Autarkis</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/i5hg0kzd7826oef/Colin%20MacLachlan.pdf?dl=0</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T13:25:02-07:00","id":937248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/934945-post-some-of-your-pcs-you-have-starting-level-please?p=937115#post937115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use the nWoD system so I'm not sure how interested you might be in the few characters I have that could be put here; but I do have two or three Vampires I could put and talk about, I think they both followed V20 or so; not nWoD at any rate. I wonder though if I should go into detail on why the stats are the way they are cuz a lot seems to be just character building without explaining why the dots are as they are. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could do that. One of those characters i posted i did have a backround wrote up for... Let me go back and see if i have them done..<br /> <br /> [Kort, Lupus Theurge]<br /> Kort was born to two Lupus kin, that were kept as school mascots/pets at a gifted students school (gifted meaning, mentally challenged). Many of the kids (and parents) felt that having the animals helped the kids out, especially those which were autistic. For a while she was overlooked by the nearby sept as a potential shifter, till one day during a gang's raid on the school (shooting up 2 teachers and 4 students), she raged out, killing all but one of the attackers. Lucky for Kort, one of the main reporters in the area was a fellow Child of Gaia kin, who managed to keep the resolution of the attack out of the main media (though some of the tabloids did have pics of the aftermath), and later several garou worked with Kort, explaining to her what she was, and felt keeping her in the school would help out.<br /> Since coming out, she has mixed her time at the school and the sept, healing when she can get away with it.. She has yet though to leave proper, to join a pack to go hunting hte wyrm, but has had several encounters with some wyrm creatures trying to infect the school..<br /> Due to her caregiver nature, she spends more time using her wits and intellect to solve problems more so than physical violence.. However she can give as good as she gets in combat if it comes to that..<br /> <br /> Unfortunately the other 3 i posted didn't have one (well one might have but the sheet is lost)..<br /> <br /> The next two i will post, will include a backround...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T14:22:18-07:00","id":937290,"title":"","content":"All my players are homid; they were first time WtA players, didn't want any of them to bite off more than they could handle; game is set in 1840s.<br /> <br /> Kefka Kevianov, 'Mocks-the-Night'<br /> Romanian American Shadow Lord Ragabash. He was sought out by a sinister Judge of Doom and inducted into the tribe of Thunder... but the telltale signs of a covert civil war being fought among the Shadow Lords makes Kefka wonder if he has chosen the right side...<br /> <br /> Zoe Kostas, 'Hears-the-Song'<br /> Greek American Iron Rider Theurge. Orphaned when her family was attacked by undead mockeries, Zoe wandered around the frontier towns with a small gang until she was taken in by a will-worker, who attempted to teach her civilized living and even some enlightened concepts before she was tracked down by her father's old pack.<br /> <br /> Zas B'ul<br /> Lipan Apache Silent Strider Philodox. His father was disgusted with the status quo among the Garou Nation and he sought to understand the Pure way of life, without threatening them or appearing as a malign influence. Zas B'ul grew up among the Lipan, and only recently was sent back east to come to grips with his heritage.<br /> <br /> Eaton 'Leper-Friend'<br /> American Bone Gnawer Galliard. The child of wayward kinfolk, Eaton's mother's Uktena lineage has been sullied by the mongrel blood of his father's family. He does his best to fight injustice, but his own rage has the propensity to get the better of him.<br /> <br /> Sylvester Clemmons, 'Rends-the-Gar'<br /> American Get of Fenris Ahroun<br /> A scion of the growing war between the Pure and the 'Wyrm Bringers,' Rends-the-Gar's family was destroyed- not by the Uktena or the Wendigo, but by his father's brutal lust for revenge. In the aftermath of a wicked slaughter, the Ahroun abandoned his father to his fate and joined a more worthy cause- purging the Wyrm from the southern territories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 07-25-2016, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T16:15:21-07:00","id":937360,"title":"","content":"I'll get to posting the first one and see what happens; enjoy the read.<br /> <br /> <b>Conrald Rimmer -- Clan Gangrel -- Camarilla</b><br /> Some dude who grew up in the rural areas of California somewhere unspecified and eventually moved into LA where the game was set in the aftermath of VtMB (with Strauss as the new Prince). He was pretty much an unemployed nobody fighting claws and teeth to keep his little apartment and feed himself and his dog 'Jackie'. Due to having a dog, he took a lot of walks mostly during after-dark where there were less people up and about, which eventually landed him the stereotypical Gangrel embrace of 'embraced and left to fend for himself'. Fortunately for him, he managed to survive long enough for the Sire to approach him and another Gangrel who was his blood-brother (played by another player) and get introduced to the Prince before they were sent on a job along with two fledgeling Nossies and Imalia babysitting them; if with some reluctance.<br /> <br /> Didn't have much time to grow, but did get along well with his 'brother' and was open towards his 'sire' if only by virtue of needing his help to adjust. Said sire seemed to be a more corporate predator than a wilds one, judging by his suit, fancy car and ghoul driver; but sadly there wasn't much more time than that to get to know him better.<br /> <br /> <b>=Attributes=</b><br /> <b>Physical: </b>Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social: </b>Charisma 2, Manipulation 2, Appearance 2<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 3, Intelligence 2, Wits 3<br /> <br /> <i>Explanation:</i> Conrald was always a physically active guy and practiced kickboxing in his past which led him to developing a good physique over the years prior to moving into the big city; he also had naturally great reflexes which leads to his notably high Dexterity score coupled with his defensive style rather than offensive. Not the smartest, but he passed school; not the most socially adept character as he is uninitiated in the finer arts of socialness but hey, if he knows someone doesn't appreciate something he can keep his ears clean when talking to them and generally can run with a script when in an otherwise unfamiliar setting.<br /> <br /> <b>=Abilities=</b><br /> <b>Talents: </b>Alertness 3, Athletics 2, Brawl 2, Dodge 3, Empathy 2, Intimidation 2, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge 1<br /> <b>Skills: </b>Animal Ken 3, Drive 1, Etiquette 1, Melee 1, Stealth 2, Survival 3<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Academics 1, Finance 1, Investigation 1, Medicine 1, Science 1<br /> <br /> <i>Explanation:</i> I don't remember too clearly what went through my head when I made these, but the Athletics, Brawl and Dodge can all be attributed to his kickboxing and gymming back in the ways. I think in hindsight Alertness and Athletics might've done well being swapped as I don't imagine him ever having specifically trained or honed his alertness but rather kinda just comes naturalish, but what can you do? Reasonably able in social situations, not the finest dancer on the floor but he's not completely helpless either. Streetwise comes primarily from his walks I imagine granting him notable area knowledge and lets him see and hear a lot on what goes around. Mental Abilities I imagine are all from his days in school; he's no star but he passed - as previously mentioned. Finance I justify with LA being fucking expensive, so he has to learn how to handle his economy if he wishes to survive in there. Speaking of, no clue what I was thinking with giving Survival 3. Maybe he liked hiking or lived in some rural area? Open-ended past and all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Animal Ken I imagine coming from always having had animals around and owning one himself, thus making him a good set of hands when it comes to managing them.<br /> <br /> <b>=Backgrounds=</b><br /> Resources 2, Contacts 2, Influence 1 (Streets)<br /> <br /> <i>Explanation:</i> Your guess is as good as mine; I don't remember clearly on this. Presumably he was on the wealthier side of things, perhaps from some well-off ranch or something? I donno. Or he might've done less than legal shit to keep himself afloat, either way that money didn't come out of nowhere. Just don't remember where. Contacts I'm guessing are people on the streets, and influence might've been better off with small-scale Fame or something as a known person around; he had a tendency to stop by for chats and hear the word on the streets, sometimes toss a buck or two around where need be. Maybe hobo favor made him influential in making them listen? I really don't remember.<br /> <br /> <b>=Virtues &amp; The Rest=</b><br /> Conscience 3, Self-Control 4, Courage 3<br /> Humanity 7, Willpower 4<br /> Animalism 1, Fortitude 1, Protean 2<br /> 13th Generation<br /> <br /> aaaaand that's about it. Want more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T22:41:53-07:00","id":937487,"title":"","content":"Ok. Next up is the glass walker, Bryon. His concept was (due to being homid), as a PI, ergo his physical and mentals need to be high, and he also needs decent combat skills (more ranged than brawl).<br /> <br /> Byron was the first of his family in 5 generations to be true born, all the rest have been kinfolk, which initially did earn him scorn scorn from his kin (especially his brother and 2 sisters), though they have mellowed out over time..During his youth, he shied away from most of the sports, preferring to join the schools JROTC program. After earning several merit awards, his kin eventually sent him to a military like academy, but upon graduation, he declined joining the military itself, instead taking up college to earn his PI license. So during the day, he attended a local law school, and at night he assisted a fellow Glass walker as a back up for his PI firm. 10 credit hours from completing his degree, news of his father's death reached him. Cops had the killer, but due to some corruption in the lab, the evidence got chucked. This secured his desire to work as a PI.<br /> His first change was VERY late coming, but when it did, it prompted a local GW theurge to bring him into the nearby sept. Knowing his clan's history, it was decided it would serve all better if he relocated, changed his name and work for a different sept, as it was feared (rightly so) he would seek out vengeance, which might tempt him too much.. Though this has not stopped his surviving kin from trying to find him.. They can be a pest at times, which has caused him to have to uproot his practice twice already.<br /> <br /> Since then, he has spent almost 4 years off and on, working as a PI, and assisting what ever pack needs a spare member. Even when in a pack, he has shown no inclination to lead it, but does act as their lawgiver.<br /> <br /> His physicals were split 3/4/3 S/D/St, with a specialty of lightning reflexes for dex. Social was 3 Ch 1 Man and 2 App. Perception and int got 3 each for mental, with 2 dots for wits (using 5 of his freebies).<br /> For abilities, he went Talents/Skills/Knowledge. For his talents, he went 2 in alertness, athletics and streetwise,, and 1 in each of intimidation, brawl, expression and primal urge, showing that he has not fully embraced his Garou side yet, and dodge rounds it out at 3 dots. <br /> Skills he went with 1 in both drive, survival and animal ken, with 2 in repair and stealth, and 3 in firearms. (2 points spent),<br /> For knowledge, he went 1 in computers, law, linguistics, rituals and occult and 2 in investigations (4 more freebies spent)<br /> Backrounds were split between resources 3 (from his job), contacts 1 (a publicist for a national tabloid), 1 rites and 2 in fetish (a gift he acquired upon being the first changer in his clan for a long time). 2 more freebies spent bringing up the total spent to 13)<br /> For Rage, he bumped his initial 1 up to 4 (3 spent), Gnosis went up from 1 to 3 (4 spent) and willpower to 5 (2 spent, bringing up the total freebies spent to 22, offset by his 7 pts of flaws).<br /> For flaws he went with, Persistent parents, Late shifter, Two mild phobias (heights and confined spaces) and a intolerance of drug dealers (the criminal who killed his father)..<br /> For his initial gifts, he chose master of fire (to offset the few times he has been in fights where fire got used), Open seal (to assist in breaking into places) and Trick shot (to assist his gunplay.<br /> For his '2 dots of fetishes, he went with 4 talens, the &quot;John woo specials (Bottomless clips)' 3 of which are used for his H&amp;K MP5 he is licensed to carry, while the last is sized for his Glock 22 pistol. His one dot of rituals went to acquire Talisman dedication (A tracksuit).. <br /> <br /> Due to his continual acting as a human more than a Garou, he has been recently nagged BY fellow glass walkers.. BUT for now, that has not bothered him much.. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}